menu "Iridium ACARS app options"

config STATUS_LOG_VERBOSE
    bool "Emit the full 8-line per-second status block"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, status_logger emits the full per-second telemetry
        block:
            USB / USB-XFR / USB-RB / Cycle / Ingest / DSP / Worker /
            Worker-stages
        Useful while tuning throughput, the DSP pipeline, or the worker
        stages — gives a complete view in one place.

        When disabled (default for production), status_logger emits one
        short line per second:
            STATUS: rate=X.XX MB/s frames=N processed=N drops=N
        plus a separate WARN line if any anomaly counter is nonzero
        (rb_full_drops, status_err, resubmit_err, worker dropped). Real
        burst/decode events (BURST DETECTED, DEMOD SUCCESS, BCH DECODE
        SUCCESS, Block1 Data) are unaffected — they always log.

        Cost of the verbose block: ~3 KB/s of serial bandwidth (~250
        MB/day on a continuous capture log) and ~2 ms of UART time per
        second on Core 1. Off by default to keep long unattended
        captures readable.

config DIAG_TASK_DUMP
    bool "Emit per-task CPU/stack dump every 5 s"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, class_driver_task calls uxTaskGetSystemState every
        5 s and emits one ESP_LOGI line per FreeRTOS task. Useful for
        diagnosing which task is hot on which core, but the call is
        expensive: malloc + N-task snapshot + N+1 log lines, all on the
        Core 0 hot path. Measured to cause a ~5-10 ms consumer stall
        once per 5 s, which lets the USB ringbuffer fill past 480 KB
        and produces clustered rb_full_drops at the 5 s boundary.

        Default off — re-enable temporarily (idf.py menuconfig) when
        actively debugging task-affinity or runtime-distribution issues.

config SMOKE_TEST_MODE
    bool "Run target-side smoke test instead of USB streaming"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, app_main runs smoke_test_run() instead of starting
        the USB host daemon and class_driver tasks. The smoke test feeds
        a synthetic noise/tone/noise IQ stream through the production
        ingest -> dsp_processor path and asserts the FFT detector raises
        a burst at the expected bin with high SNR.

        Use for functional regression checks before/after changes that
        touch the convert, signal_buffer, ingest_core1, or dsp_processor
        code. No USB device needs to be attached.

config SMOKE_TEST_CORPUS
    bool "Use the test_corpus fixture (synthetic Iridium PRBS-15 burst) instead of a synthetic tone"
    depends on SMOKE_TEST_MODE
    default n
    help
        When enabled, the smoke test uses tests/fixtures/fixture_corpus_uint8.h
        as the signal source — a synthetic Iridium PRBS-15 burst from
        test_corpus/prbs15-2M-20dB.sigmf-data, resampled to 2.56 MSPS and
        quantised to uint8 IQ. The detector should fire on the burst's
        carrier (FFT bin near DC since the corpus carrier is at the SDR
        center frequency).

        The fixture must be regenerated via tests/scripts/build_fixtures.py
        if the corpus or resampling parameters change. Without this flag,
        the smoke test uses a synthetic tone at FFT bin 200 (semantic
        regression check, not a corpus regression).

config SMOKE_TEST_FRAME_DECODER
    bool "Drive the frame_decoder task with canned post-demod bits from the Albuquerque corpus"
    depends on SMOKE_TEST_MODE
    depends on !SMOKE_TEST_CORPUS
    depends on !SMOKE_TEST_REAL_IRIDIUM
    default n
    help
        Target-side smoke test for the Phase D frame_decoder pipeline
        (frame_queue -> classifier -> [later: LCW extractor / SBD
        reassembler / libacars]). Bypasses USB ingest, ingest_core1,
        and dsp_processor; iterates over the 82 entries of
        tests/fixtures/fixture_albq_frames_corpus.h and pushes each
        directly into frame_decoder_push(). Useful for verifying that
        the on-target classifier produces the same per-class counts as
        the host regression (97.6% agreement against gr-iridium).

        Mutually exclusive with SMOKE_TEST_CORPUS and SMOKE_TEST_REAL_IRIDIUM.
        Asserts on-target counts vs the parser-expected counts embedded
        in fixture_albq_frames_corpus.h. PASS criteria:
          - All 82 frames consumed by the decoder task
          - Per-class counts (UNKNOWN / MS / TL / BC / LW.DA / LW.other)
            within ±2 of host expected (real-RF noise margin).

config SMOKE_TEST_RAW_IRIDIUM
    bool "End-to-end IQ -> ACARS smoke test using the raw-LO Albuquerque fixture"
    depends on SMOKE_TEST_MODE
    depends on !SMOKE_TEST_CORPUS
    depends on !SMOKE_TEST_FRAME_DECODER
    depends on !SMOKE_TEST_REAL_IRIDIUM
    default n
    help
        Drives the full pipeline (USB-emulated ingest -> dsp_processor
        -> worker_core1 -> qpsk_demod + BCH -> frame_decoder ->
        classifier) using a 'raw-mode' fixture: the Albuquerque cf32
        decimated to 2.56 MSPS at a fixed LO (1618.5 MHz) with NO
        per-burst pre-shift. Bursts appear at their natural frequency
        offsets in the 2.56 MHz subband, so the worker's
        peak_bin -> freq-centre chain works correctly and qpsk_demod
        can demodulate.

        Mutually exclusive with the other SMOKE_TEST_* fixture modes.
        On PASS reports per-class frame_decoder counts driven entirely
        by demod from raw IQ — closes the loop for hardware-in-the-
        loop validation without needing the antenna installed.

config SMOKE_TEST_REAL_IRIDIUM
    bool "Use the Albuquerque real-RF Iridium fixture (highest-SNR IDA-DL burst)"
    depends on SMOKE_TEST_MODE
    depends on !SMOKE_TEST_CORPUS
    default n
    help
        When enabled, the smoke test uses tests/fixtures/fixture_albq_uint8.h —
        a 30 dB SNR IDA-DL burst from
        test_data/iridium_downlink_2022-03-17_albuquerque, resampled to
        2.56 MSPS and quantised to uint8 IQ, frequency-shifted so the
        burst's carrier (1625.27 MHz absolute) lands at DC of the 2.56
        MHz subband. The detector should fire near FFT bin 1024 ± leakage,
        and the worker should produce ~382 demod bits matching the
        corresponding host-test ground truth (tests/fixtures/fixture_albq_truth.h).

        This is the hardware-in-the-loop counterpart of the host-side
        test_demod_albq regression: same source burst, same subband
        frequency shift, same end-to-end pipeline — except this one
        runs on real P4 silicon through the production ingest -> DSP ->
        worker chain. Bit-perfect agreement vs gr-iridium ground truth
        on the host implies the firmware should also produce a clean
        decode here.

        Mutually exclusive with SMOKE_TEST_CORPUS. Regenerate the
        fixture with tests/scripts/build_albq_fixture.py if you change
        the source recording or resampling parameters.

endmenu
